hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"2721","**\nNarrated to us Ya'qub ibn Ibrahim and narrated to me Yahya ibn Sa'id, both on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, from Yahya ibn 'Ubayd.\n\nAnd narrated to us Muhammad ibn Ma'mar, who said: Narrated to us Muhammad—meaning Ibn Bakr al-Bursani—who informed us Ibn Jurayj, who informed me Yahya ibn 'Ubayd, the freed slave of al-Sa'ib, that his father informed him that 'Abdullah ibn al-Sa'ib informed him that he heard the Prophet (ﷺ) saying, between the Yemeni Corner (Rukn Yamani) and the Black Stone (al-Hajar al-Aswad):\n\n*\Our Lord"","" grant us good in this world and good in the Hereafter"","" and save us from the punishment of the Fire.\""*\n\nAl-Dawraqi said: He means between the Yemeni Corner and the Black Stone.\n\nNarrated to us al-Dawraqi"","" who said: Narrated to us Abu 'Asim"","" who informed us Ibn Jurayj"","" who informed me Yahya ibn 'Ubayd"","" with a similar narration to that of Ibn Ma'mar."""""
